            <ArticleTitle>Leveraging Resources to Improve Clinical Outcomes and Teach Transitional Care Through Development of Academic-Clinical Partnerships.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>303-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NNE.0000000000000166</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nurse educators need to provide students with clinical experiences that prepare them for our rapidly changing health care environments. This article describes how nurse educators used academic and clinical resources to develop a partnership between a school of nursing and clinical entity to facilitate successful transitions from hospital to home for adult heart failure and pediatric asthma patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
